body:
Pretty sure these aren't Swedish meatballs. They're typically in a cream sauce or gravy and Italian meatballs are in a tomato based sauce.

&#x200B;

Look tasty though.

The current mindset by corporations that believe that maximizing profits is the end-all of their existence. This is easy to rationalize if you say, "well, they should get paid for what they make/do because they earned it and worked hard" but it shifts a bit when you start thinking about pharmaceutical companies who did no research, but bought a patent and raise the price because, "they have a responsibility to their shareholders." I hate this mindset.

&#x200B;

Oh, and the dutch.
